    text hook "по-англи́йски?" #2f6b8f x 500 y 470 font_size 72 hidden true

    card title "I speak Russian"

A: How do you ask someone in Russian whether they speak English, and what do you say when they ask you back?
    draw tom tom_name masha masha_name hook

B: We're back in the café: I'm the waitress, Tom is my customer, so we say вы.
    highlight masha_name

    erase hook

    draw talk

    draw talk

    draw talk

A: Говори́те means speak, so вы говори́те по-англи́йски asks: do you speak English?
    highlight talk_1_words part говорите

B: There's no word for do: a question is the plain sentence, with the voice going up.
    highlight talk_2

A: And the answer was да, немно́го: yes, a little. Да is yes, the partner of нет from lesson one.
    highlight talk_2 talk_3

B: По-англи́йски means in English, and по-ру́сски in Russian, with the same по on the front.
    highlight talk_1_words talk_2_words part ^по- effect underline

    erase talk

    hide speakers

A: Now the verb itself. About myself, I say я говорю́: I speak.
    draw p_ya v_ya g_ya

A: It brings a new letter, Ю, which says yu: it's У's twin, the way Я is А's.
    highlight v_ya part ю$ color #d0865f effect pulse

B: To a friend, I'd say ты говори́шь, with the ending ишь.
    draw p_ty v_ty g_ty

B: Ш is the sh from шесть; and the soft sign you met in пять makes no sound here.
    blocking false

    highlight v_ty part ш color #d0865f effect pulse duration 2.2

    highlight v_ty part ь$ color #d0865f effect pulse duration 3

A: About Masha, I'd say она́ говори́т, she speaks; and about me, she'd say он говори́т.
    draw p_on v_on g_on

B: And to a customer, вы говори́те: there's the те again, the вы ending from здра́вствуйте.
    draw p_vy v_vy g_vy

A: So the front, говор, never changes: the ending alone tells you who is speaking.
    blocking false

    highlight v_ya v_ty v_on v_vy part ^говор color #8f887c effect underline duration 2.4

    highlight v_ya part ю$ color #3d8a5a effect pulse duration 0.7

    highlight v_ty part ишь$ color #3d8a5a effect pulse duration 0.7

    highlight v_on part ит$ color #3d8a5a effect pulse duration 0.7

    highlight v_vy part ите$ color #3d8a5a effect pulse duration 1.2

B: And as in вода́ from lesson one, an о without the stress sounds like а: говорю́ is ga-va-RYU.
    blocking false

    highlight v_ya part о color #d0865f effect pulse duration 3.4

    draw note

    highlight note duration 2.4

    erase note

    hide table

B: But Tom and I are old friends, so outside the café we say ты.
    show speakers

    draw talk2

    draw talk2

    draw talk2

A: Ты, so говори́шь; and I answer for myself with я говорю́. Fair enough, Masha: немно́го.
    highlight talk2_1 talk2_2

    erase talk2

    hide speakers

    draw match

    ask "Match each person to the verb." on match store m reveal_style morph stage own test t1
        intro: Five questions now, then your score.
        right: Я говорю́, ты говори́шь, она́ говори́т, вы говори́те.
        wrong: You got {m} on the first try.

    erase match

    quiz "Masha tells a friend about Tom: Том … по-ру́сски. Which word fills the gap?" reveal.text "Том говори́т по-ру́сски." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 330 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 test t1
        right: Говори́т: Tom is он, and он takes the ending ит.
        wrong: She's talking about him, not to him: which row is он?
        * говорю́
        * говори́шь
        + говори́т

    erase reveal_1_stamp

    ask "A Russian asks: Вы говори́те по-ру́сски? Answer a little: type it." answer ["немного"] store a3 default немного translit true reveal.text "Да, немно́го." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 420 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 test t1
        keys: АБВГДЕЁЖЗИЙКЛМНОПРСТУФХЧШЫЬЮЯ
        right: Немно́го: a little.
        wrong: It's the word from both dialogues: немно́го.

    erase a3_stamp

    quiz "You meet a friend's grandmother. How do you ask if she speaks English?" reveal.text "Вы говори́те…?" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 290 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 test t1
        right: Вы говори́те: you've just met, and she's older, so вы.
        wrong: Would you greet her with привет or здра́вствуйте?
        * Ты говори́шь по-англи́йски?
        + Вы говори́те по-англи́йски?

    erase reveal_3_stamp

    ask "Finish the verb for ты: ты говор… Type the ending." answer ["ишь","говоришь"] store a5 default ишь translit true reveal.text "ты говори́шь" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 380 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 test t1
        keys: АБВГДЕЁЖЗИЙКЛМНОПРСТУФХЧШЫЬЮЯ
        right: Ишь: ты говори́шь, with the silent soft sign at the end.
        wrong: It sounds like ish, and ends with the soft sign.

    erase a5_stamp

    show table

A: You got {t1.score} of {t1.total}.
    results test t1 retry true pass 4

A: So one verb, four endings: говорю́, говори́шь, говори́т, говори́те, and the ending tells you who is speaking.
    blocking false

    highlight v_ya part ю$ color #3d8a5a effect pulse duration 1.3

    highlight v_ty part ишь$ color #3d8a5a effect pulse duration 1.3

    highlight v_on part ит$ color #3d8a5a effect pulse duration 1.3

    highlight v_vy part ите$ color #3d8a5a effect pulse duration 2.5

    hide table

    show speakers

B: And now you can answer the question every Russian will ask you: да, немно́го!
    box end_r "Да, немно́го!" #3d8a5a say "Да, немного!" say_voice a x 500 y 470 width 420 height 110 radius 26 font_size 58

    erase end_r

    draw bye

    draw bye

